  "solution": {
    "text": "The conditions and consequence that favour $t_{2 g}^3 e_g^1$ configuration in a metal complex are\n(i) weak field ligand, and\n(ii) high spin complex\n\nFor weak field ligands, splitting energy ( $\\Delta_0$ ) is lower than pairing energy $(P)$. As a result distribution of electrons for $3 \\mathrm{~d}^4$ will be $t_{2 \\mathrm{~g}}^3 \\mathrm{e}_{\\mathrm{g}}^1$. It results in high spin complex due to maximum number of unpaired electrons.",
    "image": null
  },
